{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-92271",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Let's check each pair in turn.\n\n- $(-1,2)$ is a solution of our equation. Indeed, substituting $x=-1$ and $y=2,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+5y & =8 \\\\ 2\\cdot (-1)+5\\cdot 2 & =8 \\\\ -2+10 & =8 \\\\ 8 & =8\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- $(-6,4)$ is a solution of our equation. Indeed, substituting $x=-6$ and $y=4,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+5y & =8 \\\\ 2\\cdot (-6)+5\\cdot 4 & =8 \\\\ -12+20 & =8 \\\\ 8 & =8\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- $(-2,1)$ is *not* a solution of our equation. Substituting $x=-2$ and $y=1,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+5y & =8 \\\\ 2\\cdot (-2)+5\\cdot 1 & =8 \\\\ -4+5 & =8 \\\\ 1 & \\ne 8\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
